Block Lists gathers what a firewall blocks by list into one page:
public address lists (Spamhaus DROP, abuse.ch Feodo Tracker, Emerging
Threats, CINS Army, blocklist.de) fetched daily into aliases, countries
in a GeoIP alias, the DNS block lists of Unbound shown beside them, and
TLS clients cut by their JA4 fingerprint from the Intrusion Detection's
log. The block rules are registered by the plugin and never added to
the owner's own rules. Connections already open to a newly listed
address are cut, and on a Sophos XGS taken out of the coprocessor.

Plugin Changelog
================

1.0.4

* Phase 2: web categories from UT1 through Unbound's own blocklist, and a
  Lookup tab
* Phase 3: what the IPS drops, blocked and cut for a while

1.0.3

* with Both ways, a device inside that tries to reach a
  command-and-control list is blocked and logged by its own address, on
  the inside interfaces; os-netreport 1.0.7's alert reads that log
* where os-xgs-npu is installed, the connections of a listed address,
  and those cut by their JA4 fingerprint, are dropped in hardware too,
  and handed back to the host when the address leaves every watched
  list; with os-xgs-npu's releases so far, which do not carry its
  hand-back yet (merged 2026-11-18), nothing is handed back and nothing
  breaks
* lists fetched every two hours, never more often than their publisher
  allows: Spamhaus DROP, Emerging Threats and CINS Army stay at once a
  day
* ThreatFox's command-and-control addresses, with the owner's abuse.ch
  Auth-Key, at the pace abuse.ch's terms allow; without a key nothing is
  fetched and the page says so

1.0.2

* an update installed only as its owner signed it: the release's
  manifest checked with the release key this plugin carries, and the
  archive's SHA-256 and size the signed ones
* the latest release's signature read by the tag its manifest names,
  and a manifest too deep to parse refused by its signature

1.0.1

* a list chosen again cuts what it names, also what was opened while it was not chosen
* only the aliases Block Lists makes are its own; an owner's alias named blocklists_* is left alone
* the JA4 watch covers the whole minute, so a fingerprint listed mid-minute is cut within seconds
* the IDS log read a line at a time; snapshots written only on a change, by one run at a time
* the rules hook is checked by php -l, before the installer copies it
* removal stops its cuts, deletes its state and empties its tables that nothing uses
* the page's menu entry carries an icon in the XGS section, and a Font Awesome 6 one in its own

1.0.0

* Initial release
